## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design NUMA-aware memory management at scale. Evaluates page migration planning, coherence, and interaction with TLB shootdowns.

## Key Concepts
- NUMA-aware balancing and migration policies
- Per-node freelists and per-VM quotas
- Synchronization and per-core work-stealing
- PTE updates, TLB coherence, and IPI coordination
- Contention, thrash, and batch processing

## Code Example
```c
// Pseudo-path sketch
void migrate_page(page_t *p, node_t *target) {
  lock(p->lock);
  if (p->state != PAGE_ONLINE) return;
  move_to_node(p, target);
  update_pte(p);
  barrier();
  tlb_shootdown(p);
  unlock(p->lock);
}
```

